messages.body_plain:
I'd like to plot multiple graphs on a single page, in such a way that the 
boxes touch along their top and bottom box lines.

I have a code snippet below that seems to work for 4 or more graphs per 
page (albeit with warning messages).  But, for 2 or 3 graphs per page, the 
graphs don't touch, and I don't get warning messages.

Can someone help me make this work for 3 graphs per page?

Thanks,

Gerry Blais

myplot <- function(graphsperpage) {
        x <- 1:100;
        graphsheet();
        for (k in 1:graphsperpage) {
                bot <- 1 - (k-1) / graphsperpage;
                top <- 1 -  k    / graphsperpage;
                par (fig=c(0.1, 0.8, top, bot));
                plot (x, x, xaxt="n",xlab="");
                }
        }

myplot(3);

